citation: |
  Derived from CMU-1-Small-Region.svs (Aperio, CC0-1.0) via wsitools
  v0.22.0-dev (main) `convert --to ome-tiff`: the pyramid is re-encoded as an
  OME-TIFF and the associated images are written faithfully (verbatim source
  strips + Predictor/JPEGTables, via opentile-go AssociatedEncoding) — a
  multi-strip JPEG thumbnail, an LZW + Predictor=2 label, and a multi-strip
  JPEG overview. Serves as opentile-go's canonical small OME-TIFF read fixture
  and the GH #23 regression case: the OME reader previously reported the LZW
  label as CompressionUnknown and truncated the multi-strip JPEGs to their
  first strip; the equivalent generic-TIFF reader (same writer) decodes all
  three correctly, and this fixture pins byte-parity between the two readers.
